                    "title": "Trends and perspectives in structural health monitoring ...",
                    "content": "## Journal of Railway Science and Technology. Volume 1, Issue 2, December 2025, Pages 59-74. # Review Trends and perspectives in structural health monitoring through edge computing: A review with zero-shot natural language processing categorization. Author links open overlay panel, , , , , , ,. The integration of edge computing into Structural Health Monitoring presents a transformative shift, overcoming limitations in latency, scalability, and centralized data processing. This review conducts a comprehensive, AI-assisted analysis of 113 peer-reviewed articles published between 2016 and 2025. Using a transformer-based Natural Language Processing model, i.e., Facehugging, the literature was automatically classified into five core research objectives, while also capturing regional and temporal trends. The review critically evaluates technological strengths, real-world deployments, and persistent challenges, offering insights into enabling factors, practical implications, and future research directions. Beyond consolidating current knowledge, this work introduces a reproducible, low-effort framework for structured, evidence-driven literature reviews in SHM. Published by Elsevier B.V. on behalf of Central South University.",
